From 42fdbb08b9b677cf60ff7b982ff76fd1f58a38f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 13:26:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: unblock of a terminal-held stale copy names
 `reopen`, which now revives it; un-walrus unblock_task

Follow-up to PR #2186 review 5891019707 (two non-blocking nits).

Nit 1: `unblock_task` refuses a blocked/scheduled/triage row whose event log holds the card done/archived
(`kanban_terminal_guard.unblock_held`), on the human paths too. The CLI then printed
`cannot unblock <id> (not blocked/scheduled?)`, which misleads: the row does read blocked/scheduled. And the
suggested remedy did not work either: `hermes kanban reopen` refused the same row ("status is 'scheduled', not
'done'; use unblock/reopen-review"), a loop with no exit.

- `kanban_terminal_guard.stale_hold` (read-only) and `unblock_refusal`: the text for that refusal, naming the
  terminal event; a held-done copy points at `hermes kanban reopen <id> --reason <why>`, an archived one says
  nothing revives it.
- CLI `kanban unblock`, the operator-call `unblock` refusal and the dashboard (single PATCH and bulk drag to
  `ready`) print it, falling back to their old text when no hold applies.
- `kanban_db_operator.reopen_done_task` also accepts a blocked/scheduled/triage row held done (`stale_hold`):
  the same reopen (re-gated landing status, descendant invalidation, `reopened` event with
  `previous_status: done` plus `stale_row_status`). A live row is still refused.

Nit 2: `unblock_task` binds `held` on its own line inside `with write_txn(conn):`, then opens
`reason_comment`. Order unchanged: evaluated in the write txn, before `precondition` and before the
reason-comment savepoint. Two lines reflowed to keep kanban_db.py at its FILE_LINES cap; plugin_api.py stays
at 2000 lines (`_open_parent_refusal` renamed `_refusal_detail`, which now covers both refusals).

Tests (tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_stale_wake_terminal.py): CLI unblock of a stale copy prints the reopen
hint and `kanban reopen` revives it; a not-held card keeps the generic message and reopen still refuses a live
row; an archived copy's text names no reopen and the dashboard echoes it. RED on main (the stale-copy and
archived tests fail; the generic-message control passes), GREEN here; 14 related files, 462 tests pass; scripts/check --base origin/main ok.
